 PHASE 6: Verify filters and Excel/PDF/HTML parity, privacy and offline operation.
 PHASE 7: Document performance, residual limitations and obtain owner approval to deploy.

 CODING DELIVERABLES:
 - Root cause report (repro steps, affected modules, source line references, evidence).
 - Minimal backward-compatible code patch with typed timestamp and formula handling.
 - Independent golden fixture tests and OOXML post-export validator.
 - Before/after report with every acceptance check PASS/FAIL/NOT_TESTED.
 - Actual exported sample workbook, PDF, HTML and local audit JSON for review.
 - Changelog, rollback plan and list of unverified external Excel behaviors.

 DEFINITION OF DONE:
 [ ] No loss of hour/minute/second information in normalized or exported timestamps.
 [ ] All supported derived columns computed correctly on all eligible rows.
 [ ] No #VALUE! or other Excel formula errors in supported generated ranges.
 [ ] SLA compliance and mean resolution match independent source fixture.
 [ ] Workbook dashboard, ledger, audit and chart values reconcile.
 [ ] Audit refuses VERIFIED when output is wrong or untested.
 [ ] Excel desktop recalc explicitly tested or honestly marked NOT_TESTED.
 [ ] Browser, Excel, PDF, HTML share same verified metric semantics.
 [ ] Sales, generic data and existing 32 templates remain working.
 [ ] Zero AI/cloud dataset processing and zero data leakage verified by network test.

